Source problem: The function $f$ has the property that for each real number $x$ in its domain, $1/x$ is also in its domain and \[
f(x) + f\left(\frac{1}{x}\right) = x.
\]What is the largest set of real numbers that can be in the domain of $f$?

(a) ${\{x\mid x\ne0\}}$

(b) ${\{x\mid x<0\}}$

(c) ${\{x\mid x>0\}}$

(d) ${\{x\mid x\ne-1\ \text{and}\ x\ne0\ \text{and}\ x\ne1\}}$

(e) ${\{-1,1\}}$
Proposed action: \]Thus if $x$ is in the domain of $f$, then $x = 1/x$, so $x = \pm 1$.
Operation: DERIVE.
